# Camera with 1141 modules of 7 pixels each.
# Each of the 7987 pixels has a size of 2.33 cm (flat-to-flat, hex. funnel hori.).
# Between pixels is a gap of 0.1 cm. Pixel spacing is 2.4 cm.
# The pixel spacing corresponds to 0.050 deg at f=28.00 m for pixel plus any gap.
# The camera is fully contained in a circle of 2.399 m diameter, corresponding to a 4.909 FoV of deg 
# The camera is fully equipped with pixels in a circle 1.956 m diameter, corresponding to a 4.000 FoV of deg 
# Funnels walls are assumed to have an average reflectivity of 78.0 percents.
# This file contains only the AnalogSumTrigger subset of trigger conditions.
# PixType format:
# Par.  1: pixel type (here always 1)
#       2: PMT type (must be 0)
#       3: cathode shape type (see below)
#       4: visible cathode diameter [cm]
#       5: funnel shape type (see below)
#       6: funnel diameter (flat-to-flat for hexagons and squares) [cm]
#       7: depth of funnel [cm]
#       8: a) funnel efficiency "filename",   b) funnel plate transparency
#       9: a) optional wavelength "filename", b) funnel wall reflectivity
# Cases a) and b) are distinguished by the format of parameter 8: a quoted
# string indicates case a) while a real number indicates case b).
# In case a) in column 8, columns 3, 4, and 7 are not used. If in case a)
# the optional file name for the wavelength dependence is provided, the
# overall scale in the file provided as parameter 8 is ignored because
# it is rescaled such that the average over all mirrors is equal to
# the given wavelength dependent value.
#
# Shape types: 0: circ., 1: hex(flat x), 2: sq., 3: hex(flat y)

PixType 1   0  1 0.944   1 2.33 3.670 "CTA-LST_lightguide_eff_SST1M.dat"

# Camera rotation angle [deg].
# New Keyword: Requires 2012-08-21 or newer sim_telarray AND hessio[xxx].
# Rotates the whole camera with all the pixels by the given angle.
# Note that Hillas parameters are given in the de-rotated system
# to avoid portability issues of analysis programs.
